<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banu Gómez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th–11th centuries</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Banu Gómez were a powerful noble family of the Kingdom of León, counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saldana">Saldaña</a>, Carrión and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liebana">Liébana</a> on the upper Carrión river. Descended from Count Diego Muñoz, they often rebelled against the Leonese kings and at times allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almanzor">Almanzor</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> in the late tenth century. Their power faded in the eleventh century, when Carrión passed to other families.</p></div>
